oist with her debut EP Agassy, released on November 8, 2023 through BRD Communications.","title":"Soojin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soojin"}},"Q625737":{"id":"Q625737","name":"Kenzie","ko":"켄지","birthName":"김연정","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Kim Yeon-jung"],"birth":"1976-02-03","death":"","birthplace":"Shimane Prefecture","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["songwriter","record producer"],"debut":"2002","agencies":[{"name":"SM Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483938","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/kzlab99/","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0SJw8hRAebjFomQPGcAW5e","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/2997113e-cc84-4a0c-8111-d0648b42b4dc"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Kim Yeon-jung, known professionally as Kenzie (켄지), is a South Korean songwriter and record producer signed under SM Entertainment. She has written and produced songs for SM artists such as BoA, Isak N Jiyeon, Super Junior, The Grace, TVXQ, Girls' Generation, Shinee, f(x), Exo, Red Velvet, SuperM, Aespa, NCT, Riize and Hearts2Hearts, as well as non-SM artists such as Twice, CIX, BAE173, The Boyz, Zerobaseone and TWS.","title":"Kenzie (songwriter)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kenzie_%28songwriter%29"}},"Q73817097":{"id":"Q73817097","name":"Dalyn","ko":"달린","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Lee So-hyun"],"birth":"1999-08-27","death":"","birthplace":"South Korea","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q73795501","name":"ANS","start":"2019","end":""}],"links":{},"photo":null,"bio":null,"positions":["Main rapper","Main dancer"],"factSources":{"positions":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%EB%8B%AC%EB%A6%B0"}}},"Q97352009":{"id":"Q97352009","name":"So Jung-hwan","ko":"소정환","birthName":"소정환","birthNameEn":"","aliases":[],"birth":"2005-02-18","death":"","birthplace":"","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2020","agencies":[{"name":"YG Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q50595","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q61057550","name":"Treasure","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/fec07f01-e5f0-4f95-88a2-97b81f9990ca"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Treasure is a South Korean boy band formed by YG Entertainment in 2019. The group consists of ten members: Choi Hyun-suk, Jihoon, Yoshi, Junkyu, Yoon Jae-hyuk, Asahi, Doyoung, Haruto, Park Jeong-woo, and So Jung-hwan. Treasure was originally composed of 12 members; Mashiho and Bang Ye-dam departed from the group in November 2022. The group debuted in 2020 with the single album The First Step: Chapter One, beginning a four-part The First Step series that also includes Chapter Two, Chapter Three, and the full-length compilation The First Step: Treasure Effect (2021).","title":"So Jung hwan","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/So_Jung_hwan"},"positions":["Vocalist","Dancer"],"mbti":"ENFP","factSources":{"positions":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%EC%86%8C%EC%A0%95%ED%99%98%28%ED%8A%B8%EB%A0%88%EC%A0%80%29"},"mbti":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%EC%86%8C%EC%A0%95%ED%99%98%28%ED%8A%B8%EB%A0%88%EC%A0%80%29"}}}}}